Z||000000||bilbo||01-16-2001||04:30 PM||||My sources tell me that the lightest fiero is the 1987 fiero gt.Anybody want to disagree with me please feel free!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||01-16-2001||04:41 PM||||I'd guess the lightest Fiero with the 2.8 would be a base '88 Formula without A/C, or if you could find one, maybe a basic 85 SE.<P>Most SE's and almost all GT's were loaded with great (but heavy) options like power windows and locks and A/C.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-16-2001||05:30 PM||||Gotta agree with Chad.  Most of the Formulas were stripped models with the V6 and WS6 suspension.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||01-16-2001||06:34 PM||||Although I didn't know it at the time, I have had a lot of people tell me that my Formula is the lightest V6 Fiero.  According to the GM Long-Lead press kits in 88, the Formula's curb weight was 2743, and the GT's 2790.  The 87 GT was 2708.  In 86 its listed at 2696, SE 2531 (prolly with a Duke).  <P>The difference that jumps out at me was between the 87 GT and 88 GT with an 82 pund difference.  Could this be from the 88 suspension?  Or maybe just more standard options?  <P>But anyway, it looks like an unoptioned 86 GT may be the lightest (SE's aside, their curbs are based on the duke engine)<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||01-16-2001||07:00 PM||||Wasn't there a 2m6 as well.  I would think since it would not be a GT or SE it would have less options and therefor lighter. <P>There was a 2m6 wasn't there, or am i incorrect.  What were the years for it<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||01-16-2001||07:16 PM|||| I read that the 1985 GT was the lightest folowed by the 86 2m6 by like 10 lbs. I look for the pages and post them later. the '88 Formulas where weighted down by being a '88<P>my old '84 SE (now Hank is Here's) was totaly guted and tiped the scales @ just under 2000lbs (land fill scale my t be accurate)||||reg||1
